O:8:"stdClass":8:{s:5:"title";s:61:"Ocean upwelling becoming more intense with a changing climate";s:4:"link";s:102:"https://environment.uw.edu/news/2014/07/ocean-upwelling-becoming-more-intense-with-a-changing-climate/";s:11:"description";s:584:"<div>Our Washington coastline is one of the most prolific and productive in the world, teeming with abundant plant and animal life. In fact, much of entire U.S. west coast is the same, and we can largely thank a strong upwelling system for driving this bounty. New research published in Science has shown that upwelling in the eastern boundary current systems &ndash; meaning, the eastern edges of ocean basins across the globe where winds, currents, and geological formations create a prime environment for upwelling &ndash; has increased globally over the past 60 years.&nbsp;</div>";s:6:"author";O:16:"SimplePie_Author":3:{s:4:"name";s:10:"John Meyer";s:4:"link";N;s:5:"email";N;}s:4:"date";s:19:"2014-07-02 22:28:12";s:10:"enclosures";a:1:{i:0;O:19:"SimplePie_Enclosure":27:{s:7:"bitrate";N;s:8:"captions";N;s:10:"categories";N;s:8:"channels";N;s:9:"copyright";N;s:7:"credits";N;s:11:"description";N;s:8:"duration";N;s:10:"expression";N;s:9:"framerate";N;s:7:"handler";N;s:6:"hashes";N;s:6:"height";N;s:10:"javascript";N;s:8:"keywords";N;s:4:"lang";N;s:6:"length";N;s:4:"link";N;s:6:"medium";N;s:6:"player";N;s:7:"ratings";N;s:12:"restrictions";a:1:{i:0;O:21:"SimplePie_Restriction":3:{s:12:"relationship";s:5:"allow";s:4:"type";N;s:5:"value";s:7:"default";}}s:12:"samplingrate";N;s:10:"thumbnails";N;s:5:"title";N;s:4:"type";N;s:5:"width";N;}}s:7:"src_url";s:102:"https://environment.uw.edu/news/2014/07/ocean-upwelling-becoming-more-intense-with-a-changing-climate/";s:8:"src_name";s:54:"Ocean upwelling becoming more intense with a chang ...";}